{"name":"Fish Pond","hex":"#86c8ed","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fish pond","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of fishpond."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fish_pond"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fish pond","blocks":[{"text":"A fish pond or fishpond is a controlled pond, small artificial lake or retention basin that is stocked with fish and is used in aquaculture for fish farming, for recreational fishing, or for ornamental purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Design_for_a_Fish-Pond_in_Plan_and_Section_MET_DP820524.jpg/330px-Design_for_a_Fish-Pond_in_Plan_and_Section_MET_DP820524.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish_pond","wikidata":"Q1265665"},{"title":"Fish","blocks":[{"text":"A fish is an aquatic, anamniotic, gill-bearing vertebrate animal with a tough cranium to protect the brain, but lacking limbs with digits. Fish can be grouped into the more basal jawless fish and the more common jawed fish, the latter including all living cartilaginous and bony fish, as well as the extinct placoderms and acanthodians. Tetrapods are descended from fish, so in a break from the long tradition of grouping all fish into a single class (Pisces), modern phylogenetics views fish as a paraphyletic group that includes all vertebrates except tetrapods. To treat fish as a monophyletic group, one would have to classify tetrapods as a clade/subgroup of specialized fish, which would make \"fish\" and \"vertebrates\" synonyms. In English, the plural of \"fish\" is fish when referring to individuals and fishes when referring to species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Balantiocheilos_melanopterus_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_02_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Balantiocheilos_melanopterus_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish","wikidata":"Q152"},{"title":"Pond","blocks":[{"text":"A pond is a small, still, land-based body of water formed by pooling inside a depression, either naturally or artificially. A pond is smaller than a lake and there are no official criteria distinguishing the two, although defining a pond to be less than 5 hectares in area, less than 5 metres (16 ft) in depth and with less than 30% of its area covered by emergent vegetation helps in distinguishing the ecology of ponds from those of lakes and wetlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Cornjum%2C_Martenastate_010.jpg/330px-Cornjum%2C_Martenastate_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pond","wikidata":"Q12719646"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Daye-pond-system-fishermen-0077.jpg/500px-Daye-pond-system-fishermen-0077.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Daye-pond-system-fishermen-0077.jpg/1280px-Daye-pond-system-fishermen-0077.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Daye-pond-system-fishermen-0077.jpg/500px-Daye-pond-system-fishermen-0077.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fishing in a fish pond system at Daye Lake near Daye, China","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaye-pond-system-fishermen-0077.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/00_Ixelles_-_Abbaye_-_La_Cambre_1.JPG/500px-00_Ixelles_-_Abbaye_-_La_Cambre_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/00_Ixelles_-_Abbaye_-_La_Cambre_1.JPG/1280px-00_Ixelles_-_Abbaye_-_La_Cambre_1.JPG